**Sec. 60001**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds previously made available to carry out Section 132 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7432). This action effectively eliminates remaining federal funding designated for clean heavy-duty vehicle programs.

**Sec. 60002**
This section repeals Section 134 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7434), which established the Greenhouse Gas Reduction Fund. It also rescinds all unobligated balances of amounts that were made available to carry out this repealed section prior to the enactment of this Act.

**Sec. 60003**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60104 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding specifically allocated for diesel emissions reduction initiatives.

**Sec. 60004**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60105 of Public Law 117-169. This action eliminates remaining federal funding designated for general air pollution reduction efforts.

**Sec. 60005**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60106 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding specifically allocated for addressing air pollution in schools.

**Sec. 60006**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 135 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7435). This action eliminates remaining federal funding for the Low Emissions Electricity Program.

**Sec. 60007**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60108 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding associated with Section 211(o) of the Clean Air Act.

**Sec. 60008**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60109 of Public Law 117-169. This action eliminates remaining federal funding designated for the implementation of the American Innovation and Manufacturing Act.

**Sec. 60009**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60110 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding for environmental enforcement technology and public information initiatives.

**Sec. 60010**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60111 of Public Law 117-169. This action eliminates remaining federal funding designated for greenhouse gas corporate reporting programs.

**Sec. 60011**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60112 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding for environmental product declaration assistance.

**Sec. 60012**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out subsections (a) and (b) of Section 136 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7436), which relates to methane emissions and waste reduction incentives for petroleum and natural gas systems. Additionally, it amends Section 136(g) of the Clean Air Act to extend the program's period by striking "calendar year 2024" and inserting "calendar year 2034."

**Sec. 60013**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 137 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7437). This action eliminates remaining federal funding for greenhouse gas air pollution plans and implementation grants.

**Sec. 60014**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60115 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding designated for the Environmental Protection Agency's efficient, accurate, and timely reviews.

**Sec. 60015**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60116 of Public Law 117-169. This action eliminates remaining federal funding for low-embodied carbon labeling for construction materials.

**Sec. 60016**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 138 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7438). This eliminates remaining federal funding for environmental and climate justice block grants.

**Sec. 60017**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60301 of Public Law 117-169. This action eliminates remaining federal funding designated for Endangered Species Act (ESA) recovery plans.

**Sec. 60018**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60401 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding for environmental and climate data collection efforts.

**Sec. 60019**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 177 of Title 23 of the United States Code. This action eliminates remaining federal funding for the Neighborhood Access and Equity Grant Program.

**Sec. 60020**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60502 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding designated for Federal building assistance.

**Sec. 60021**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60503 of Public Law 117-169. This action eliminates remaining federal funding for low-carbon materials for Federal buildings.

**Sec. 60022**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 60504 of Public Law 117-169. This eliminates remaining federal funding for the General Services Administration's (GSA) emerging and sustainable technologies programs.

**Sec. 60023**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 178 of Title 23 of the United States Code. This action eliminates remaining federal funding for environmental review implementation.

**Sec. 60024**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out Section 179 of Title 23 of the United States Code. This eliminates remaining federal funding for low-carbon transportation materials grants.

**Sec. 60025**
This section appropriates $256,657,000 from the Treasury for fiscal year 2025, available until September 30, 2029, for the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts. These funds are designated for capital repair, restoration, maintenance backlog, and security structures of the building and site. No more than 3 percent of these funds may be used for administrative costs.

**Sec. 60026**
This section amends the National Environmental Policy Act of 1969 to allow project sponsors to opt-in to paying fees for the preparation or supervision of environmental assessments or environmental impact statements. The Council on Environmental Quality must notify sponsors of the fee amount within 15 days, which is set at 125 percent of anticipated preparation or supervision costs. Projects paying these fees must complete environmental assessments within 180 days of payment and environmental impact statements within one year of the notice of intent. [end of text]


